 {:seon.task/name "an-agents-proofs-namespace-stays-a-test"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-11-11 by the Tests session (finding 12's sweep, jolt/tests-agentproof). An agent's namespace made at its REPL gets a file by its name (```seon.source/namespace-path```: a -test suffix goes under test/, anything else under src/), so a proofs-only namespace like lab.proofs is written back under src/, root loads it after a merge (```seon.program/test-nss```, loadable), and ```seon.program/program-names``` counts its test vars as program in a task's write set. The catch law now tells a test by its :test fact (:var/meta), not its file. Correct: the same fact decides the rest: a namespace whose every var is a deftest is a test namespace wherever its file is, written under test/ and never loaded by root. Proof: an agent's lab.proofs with only deftests is written under test/ and not in program-names."
